    "android_apple_local": "unavailable on this Linux builder (no NDK, no Apple targets)",
    "cpu_local": "dated exact-head Linux CI create_group rows; candidate faster on every collected row, no >5% slowdown",
    "linux_ci_on_f469eb912664fc274734bcbe150eaefe97e72949": "Linux Android and host profile measurements succeeded; Android primary ARM ABIs shrank 19-22 percent; report sha256 e0ddbd525e0b0b7a6cc210be510b78d422d5545e877fa17136a62683dc09438c",
    "macos_ci_on_f469eb912664fc274734bcbe150eaefe97e72949": "Apple slices measured (+85 percent archive growth) then Validate Apple archives failed on compiler_builtins __LLVM,__bitcode; report sha256 16a485692a20cf406f0aba644666cadd457e9cb996c083df3ef27df984b616e8",
    "apple_growth_investigation": "Growth matches Apple rustc default embed-bitcode=yes (native+bitcode) plus a leftover 0xe80 __LLVM,__bitcode section in the Rust 1.97.1 iOS compiler_builtins rlib. Exact-head macOS CI on 2c1fd5b97bd16c9577e18a795564579c2902f909 then failed sanitization because those leftovers live as MH_OBJECT section fields inside a parent __TEXT load command. Exact-head macOS CI on e9fb5a8f577d2c6352d12eebf76111afbe8d6e01 then failed with unknown Mach-O load command 0x25 (LC_VERSION_MIN_IPHONEOS) after mid-file bitcode removal. This revision disables embed-bitcode on Apple Cargo invocations and sanitizes leftover Mach-O bitcode segments and section-level __LLVM leftovers without whitelisting members, while keeping offset-free load commands intact. This revision also merges origin/master 7d8bba365def75a66774f2b2036f839411010001. Profile-affecting MarmotKit sources and these dated bytes are unchanged except for that sanitizer repair. Fresh exact-head CI is required after publication."
  },
